      'description': "Get the files of several documents as one ZIP archive, attached as an embedded resource. The archive comes as MCP content after a JSON report (file name, size, delivered), not saved on the server's machine. An archive over the server's download limit (512 KiB unless the administrator changed it) is not attached: delivered is false and the note says what to do. With offset you get one part of an archive of up to 2 GiB: start with offset=0, then repeat the arguments that next in the report names until next_offset is null, append the parts and compare the SHA-256 of the whole with checksum. Paperless builds the archive anew for every part; if a document changed in between, start again. The archive holds the newest version of each document. The whole request fails if one document is hidden from the user. Use download_document for one file.",
