    dict({
      '_meta': dict({
        'fastmcp': dict({
          'tags': list([
            'pdf',
          ]),
        }),
      }),
      'annotations': dict({
        'destructiveHint': True,
        'idempotentHint': False,
        'openWorldHint': False,
        'readOnlyHint': False,
        'title': 'Merge documents',
      }),
      'description': "Merge PDF documents, in the order given, into one new document. The new document takes the metadata (title with ' (merged)', tags, correspondent, ...) of metadata_document_id if given. The originals stay unless delete_originals is true: they then move to the Paperless trash (restore_from_trash of the trash toolset, or the web UI, restores them), which needs confirm. Without it a dialog, or an error for you to show the user, first names the documents and what would happen (see confirm). A document that could not be merged is refused first. A merge is always a new document; to make it a version, merge and then use merge_documents_as_versions (toolset versions), which absorbs the merged document for good. Originals are trashed last, by this server: only once everything was made, has the pages it should have and nothing changed meanwhile. Otherwise they stay (trashed_ids, message) and next names the calls that finish the work: look there before repeating a call. Paperless does the work later, in background tasks: the result lists the ones it could find (state, produced_ids: the new documents, or for a new version its id) and with wait_seconds waits for them. Needs the permission to change and to add documents and a change grant on (or ownership of) every document; delete_originals also needs ownership of them and the permission to delete documents. Takes PDF files; other files need archive_fallback and an archive PDF.",
      'inputSchema': dict({
        'additionalProperties': False,
        'properties': dict({
          'archive_fallback': dict({
            'default': False,
            'description': 'true merges the archive PDF of documents whose file is not a PDF.',
            'type': 'boolean',
          }),
          'confirm': dict({
            'default': False,
            'description': 'Must be true to go ahead at once. Without it a client that can show dialogs asks the user, and the tool runs only if they accept; with any other nothing changes and the error says what would happen. Describe that to the user and pass true only once they agree, or if they already asked for exactly this.',
            'type': 'boolean',
          }),
          'delete_originals': dict({
            'default': False,
