    dict({
      '_meta': dict({
        'fastmcp': dict({
          'tags': list([
            'trash',
          ]),
        }),
      }),
      'annotations': dict({
        'idempotentHint': True,
        'openWorldHint': False,
        'readOnlyHint': True,
        'title': 'List trash',
      }),
      'description': '''
        List what was deleted and can still be restored: documents and deleted versions.
        
        An entry has an id (pass it to get_trash_entry, get_trashed_file, restore_from_trash or
        empty_trash), the title and the time it was deleted. A version deleted from a document is an
        entry of its own, with version_of set to the document; while the document itself is in the
        trash, its entry covers the versions. You see the entries of documents you own or that have no
        owner; a superuser sees every entry. Filters are combined with AND. They look at up to 1000
        entries (100 if their texts are over 64 MiB or reading them is slow or fails): truncated is true
        when the trash holds more, and the notice says how to go on; ids also looks beyond them. web_url
        is the trash page of the web UI. count is the total; pass next_page as page to see more. Needs
        the permission to view documents.
      ''',
      'inputSchema': dict({
        'additionalProperties': False,
        'properties': dict({
          'deleted_from': dict({
            'anyOf': list([
              dict({
                'format': 'date',
                'type': 'string',
              }),
              dict({
                'type': 'null',
              }),
            ]),
            'default': None,
            'description': 'Deleted on this day (UTC) or later.',
          }),
          'deleted_to': dict({
            'anyOf': list([
              dict({
                'format': 'date',
                'type': 'string',
              }),
              dict({
                'type': 'null',
              }),
            ]),
            'default': None,
            'description': 'Deleted on this day (UTC) or earlier.',
